   syntax: #command [<command> <function>]
   With no arguments, prints all commands available.
   With two arguments it adds a new command.

   <function> is in the format of module.function .  Lyntin will
   tell you if the function is not callable.

   The function needs to have the signature:
      def func(words, input, seslist)

   Look at examples in player.py .

   see also: uncommand
